DISTRIBUTION ARCHITECTURE NOTICE:
This distribution separates the open benchmark reproduction harnesses (`reproduce_all.sh`)
and integration adapters (governed by their respective open-source SPDX license headers)
from the precompiled, stripped WebAssembly (`bin/silicium_dom.wasm`), Pure V8
(`sdk/silicium_v8_dom.mjs`), and section-header-obliterated ELF64 (`e_shoff=0`,
release asset `libsilicium_dom_arena.so`) native compute binaries governed by SCSL-1.0.

1. GRANT OF SINGLE-NODE EVALUATION & DEVELOPER SAFE-HARBOR LICENSE (TIER 0)
   Subject to strict compliance with all eight (8) protection shields below, The Authors
   ("Licensor") hereby grant you a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable,
   non-sublicensable, revocable, royalty-free license to execute the unmodified
   evaluation binaries ("Tier 0 Community Edition", zero license key required) solely for:
   a. Individual non-commercial benchmark verification, academic research, and peer
      performance reproduction;
   b. Single-developer local workstation, personal container (`0.0.0.0` inside local
      Docker/Podman port-mapped to `127.0.0.1` or a private single-household non-commercial
      RFC 1918 LAN), and integration testing (`127.0.0.1` / `localhost` or personal Homelab,
      `1` node, `<= 8` vCPUs, `<= 10 GiB/h` rolling evaluation envelope, `<= 16,384` active rows,
      `Queue-Depth=1`); and
   c. Automated ephemeral continuous-integration test suites (`CI=true`, unit tests,
      and Docker image verification builds) that do not serve live or commercial traffic.
   Any commercial production deployment or higher-capacity enterprise usage requires an
   active Commercial Enterprise License issued by Licensor (`silicium369@gmail.com`).

2. SHIELD 1 — NO REVERSE ENGINEERING OR BINARY DECOMPILATION
   Except to the extent expressly mandated by non-waivable applicable law, you may not
   decompile, disassemble, reverse-engineer, reconstruct stripped ELF64/Mach-O/PE section
   headers (`e_shoff = 0`), attach dynamic binary instrumentation, debuggers, or tracers
   (`ptrace`, `LD_PRELOAD`, Frida, Intel PIN, DynamoRIO), or extract internal lookup
   tables (LUTs), SIMD shuffle masks, or constants from the Software.

