6. SHIELD 5 — TECHNOLOGICAL PROTECTION MEASURES (TPMs)
   The stripped ELF64 (`e_shoff=0`) and signed Mach-O64 (`LC_CODE_SIGNATURE`) binary
   format, integrity guards, and offline Ed25519 / U256 license verification gates
   constitute Technological Protection Measures under the WIPO Copyright Treaty (WCT
   Article 11), 17 U.S.C. Section 1201, EU Directive 2001/29/EC Article 6, and applicable
   laws. Circumventing, patching, or bypassing these controls is strictly prohibited.

7. SHIELD 6 — AI-ASSISTED SYNTHESIS & CLEAN-ROOM RESTRICTIONS
   You shall NOT feed, expose, or provide the binaries, their C-ABI signatures,
   disassembly listings, control-flow graphs, PMU hardware counter traces, or timing
   profiles into any Large Language Model (LLM), AI coding agent, neural decompiler,
   automated program superoptimizer, or binary-to-binary translation layer to synthesize
   clean-room functional specifications, train models, or transpile kernels to another
   instruction set architecture (ISA).

8. SHIELD 7 — SINGLE-NODE COMMUNITY SCOPE, DEVELOPER SAFE-HARBOR & CLUSTER LIMITS
   Evaluation is bounded to one (1) physical CPU socket and one (1) physical GPU
   accelerator with `Queue-Depth=1` (`<= 8` vCPUs, `<= 10 GiB/h` rolling throughput, and
   `<= 16,384` active rows in library/SDK mode).
   a. Developer Loopback, Personal Container/Homelab & Ephemeral CI Safe-Harbor:
      Single-developer local testing on loopback (`127.0.0.1` / `localhost`), personal
      non-commercial single-household container binding (`0.0.0.0` inside local
      Docker/Podman mapped exclusively to `127.0.0.1` or a private single-household
      RFC 1918 LAN on `1` node within the `<= 8` vCPUs, `<= 10 GiB/h`, `<= 16,384` active
      rows envelope), and automated ephemeral test runners (`CI=true`, `GITHUB_ACTIONS=true`,
      unit test suites, and non-serving Docker build checks) are expressly permitted
      without a license key.
   b. Commercial Proxy & External Multi-User Network Ban: Outside the single-developer
      loopback and personal single-household container/Homelab safe-harbor in Section 8a,
      you shall NOT bind or expose the binary on external, corporate, or shared network
      interfaces (`0.0.0.0` in corporate/cloud/multi-user environments, Kubernetes Ingress,
      NGINX, Envoy, gRPC, or multi-user HTTP gateways), IPC queues, or shared-memory
      multiplexers to serve multiple users, employees, tenants, or production workers
      without a Commercial Enterprise License (`Slots 2..10`).
   c. Commercial Production & Unlicensed Cluster Use: You shall NOT deploy the binary in
      any commercial production service, revenue-generating SaaS, internal corporate batch
      pipeline, or unlicensed cluster workload, nor recycle containers, processes, or
      `/dev/shm` state to reset the `10 GiB/h` evaluation cap, without an active
      Commercial Enterprise License (`Slots 2..10`) from Licensor.

9. SHIELD 8 — ENTERPRISE COMPLIANCE IDENTIFICATION & PUBLIC BENCHMARKING
   a. Enterprise Compliance Identification: All headers carry `SPDX-License-Identifier:
      LicenseRef-Silicium-Community-1.0` so enterprise Software Composition Analysis (SCA)
      tooling (Black Duck, FOSSA, Snyk) accurately classifies the binary license and
      enforces organizational compliance policies unless a Commercial Enterprise License
      certificate is registered.
   b. Public Benchmarks & Competitive Evaluation: Independent public benchmarks of the
      unmodified Software are welcomed when citing `reproduce_all.sh` and exact hardware
      configurations for reproducibility. You may not use the Software to calibrate,
      autotune, train, or validate a competing commercial engine.

